  "term": "Psychological First Aid",
  "definition": "Psychological first aid is an early psychosocial approach used during or after traumatic events such as disasters, accidents, or terrorist attacks that have harmful effects on a person or on society. It centers on identifying basic physical and mental needs in people involved in major events.",
